WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.580
Imran Khan, a cricket star turned politician, is Pakistan's likely next Prime Minister.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:17.120
Khan has used an anti-corruption platform to build a mass following, but he has hardly gotten to where he is on his own.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.360
Khan's main opponent,

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.180
former Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif,

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.360
was thrown out of office in 2017 on dubious charges by the Supreme Court.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:28.040
Since then, he has received a 10-year prison sentence for corruption

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.600
and was arrested along with his daughter and political heir Maryam Nawaz Sharif.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.020
Nawaz Sharif has been a vocal critic of Pakistan's army.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:41.440
Many believe that the army worked to throw him out and promote its preferred candidate, Imran Khan.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.600
Khan's use of the army to get elected does not bode well for Pakistan's ailing democracy.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.400
His worldview combines socialism and Islamism.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:57.300
He blames America for Pakistan's terrorist problem, supports fundamentalist positions, and wants Pakistan to be an Islamic welfare state.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.880
With a struggling economy and decaying international reputation,

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:06.500
Pakistan needs introspection. Imran Khan represents a doubling down on denial.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:12.580
What do you think about Imran Khan? Will he weaken or strengthen Pakistan's democracy?

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.520
Let us know in your comments.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.320
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.400
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

